ct patient mortality?</article-title><source>J Gen Intern Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1525-1497.2004.30336.x</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Howard D, Silber J, Jobes D. Do regulations limiting residents&#x02019;s work hours affect patient mortality? J Gen Intern Med. 2004;19:1&#x02013;7. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14748854</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fletcher</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Underwood</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Davis</surname><given-names>SQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Mangrulkar</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>McMahon</surname><given-names>LF</given-names></name><name><surname>Saint</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Systematic review: effects of resident work hours on patient safety</article-title><source>Ann Intern Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>141</volume><issue>11</issue><fpage>851</fpage><lpage>857</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Fletcher KE, Underwood W III, Davis SQ, Mangrulkar RS, McMahon LF Jr., Saint S. Systematic review: effects of resident work hours on patient safety. Ann Intern Med. 2004;141(11):851&#x02013;7. <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15583227</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vidyarthi</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><name><surname>Katz</surname><given-names>PP</given-names></name><name><surname>Wall</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><name><surname>Wachter</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Auerbach</surname><given-names>AD</given-names></name></person-group><article-